From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: MihawkGen, a second frame generator: 40 fps shown at 120

prospero-win 345a71b (#722) vendors Mihawk's PS5 MihawkGen
(third_party/mihawkgen, GPL-3.0-or-later) and wraps a game's swapchain with
it when PW_FRAMEGEN is 2 to 4: that many pictures for each frame, FIFO
pacing them. PC5 already has a pw_framegen.cpp, its own FSR3 frame
generation, so MihawkGen's shim comes as pw_mihawkgen.cpp, .h and _vk.h,
its names changed to pw_mihawkgen_* and pw_mgvk_*, linked into
libvulkan.prx beside PC5's (tools/link_radv_prx.sh), and asked after it in
the lookups (pw_vulkan_radv.c). PC5 sets only one of PW_PC5_FRAMEGEN and
PW_FRAMEGEN for a game.

PC5 uses it at factor 3: 40 fps shown at 120 on a 119.88 Hz display. On
59.94 Hz three pictures a frame would hold a game at 20 fps, so there a
swapchain gets two, 30 -> 60 (chain_factor). The profile's [display]
framegen key of upstream's change isn't taken: PC5 sets the environment.
